
VSAN

All the physical ESXi server storages are combined and configured together for a VSAN ( Raw disks are mounted)
To configure Raid 5 and Raid 6 in VSAN requires a flash SSD 
Single SSD which acts as a cache for repeated operations (read/write) is used for read and write opearation for and the remaing HDD
acts as read and wrtie for general operations. 


Default Storage polices:

PFFT = 1 (Primary Failures To Tolerate) #The VM can survive one host, disk group, or disk failure depending on the failure domain configuration. Typically implemented as RAID-1 mirroring in a 3-node cluster)
Stripe Width = 1 # Data is stored as a single stripe. No additional striping is requested for performance optimization. This is the default and recommended setting in most environments)
Flash Read Cache Reservation = 0 #No dedicated flash cache is reserved for this VM. The VM uses the shared cache pool dynamically)
Object Space Reservaton = 0 # Thin provisioning. Storage space is consumed only as data is written, rather than reserving the entire VMDK size upfront
Force Provisioning = No # vSAN will not create the object if policy requirements cannot be met. It prevents non-compliant VM provisioning



